In this scenario, both girls are pulling on the rope with the same force but in opposite directions. According to Newton's third law, the force exerted by each girl on the rope is equal in magnitude and opposite in direction to the force exerted by the rope on each girl. 

Since both girls are pulling with the same force, the net force acting on each girl is zero. This is because the forces exerted by each girl on the rope are equal and opposite, resulting in no net force acting on each girl.

