(C) use carbon and release oxygen: This option is correct because plants absorb carbon dioxide (a form of carbon) and release oxygen as a byproduct of photosynthesis.

(D) use carbon and release nitrogen: This option is incorrect because plants don't release nitrogen as a byproduct of photosynthesis. Nitrogen is a separate element that is cycled through the environment through other processes.

